<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Act of Free Choice</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1969</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Act of Free Choice was the process in July and August 1969 by which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> sought to confirm its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-new-guinea">West New Guinea</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Agreement of 1962. Instead of a general vote, 1,025 selected representatives voted unanimously, under Indonesian military pressure, to remain part of Indonesia. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> took note of the result, but many Papuans and outside observers regard it as invalid.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/act-of-free-choice.jpg" alt="Act of Free Choice" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Central Intelligence Agency, United States of America · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indonesia_2002_CIA_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
